Ren is a native reader for the News app of Nextcloud. It syncs the
feeds, folders and articles of your Nextcloud, and whether you read or
starred them, and works from its own copy, also offline. Articles are
shown as the feed sends them; the web page behind an article opens in a
tab, rendered by Servo (in a helper program, started only then), with
ads and trackers blocked.

It needs Rust 1.92 or newer (rust-opt, or rustup), and to build Servo's
JavaScript engine from its source clang with libclang, Python 3 and a
C++ compiler, which a full Slackware installation has. The build is
offline: the second download holds the crates. Building Servo takes
a while and several GB of disk; WITHOUT_SERVO=yes builds without web
page tabs (pages then open in the browser):

  WITHOUT_SERVO=yes ./ren.SlackBuild

The app password for your Nextcloud is kept in the Secret Service
(KWallet, or GNOME Keyring), or comes from a command set in the settings
(password-command).
